  "knowledge": {
    "progressSummary": "COMPLETE: dual q-Pascal + full reflection symmetry proved (verified, 0-axiom, 4 thm/183L). Resolves 2 of parent oq-02-oq-02-oq-01 open items.",
    "builtItems": [
      "qBinomial_ratio (BinomialTheoremOQ02OQ02OQ01OQ03.lean:70): (q^{k+1}-1)qBinom(n,k+1)=(q^{n-k}-1)qBinom(n,k), induction on n, k=0 base = geom_sum_mul telescoping.",
      "qBinomial_dual_pascal (:101): qBinom(n+1,k+1)=qBinom(n,k+1)+q^{n-k}qBinom(n,k) via recurrence + ratio (one-line linear_combination).",
      "qBinomial_reflection (:114): qBinom(n,k)=qBinom(n,n-k) for k<=n; ordinary recurrence on left endpoint + dual on right endpoint coincide up to add_comm after IH.",
      "qBinomial_choose_symm (:142): q=1 specialization recovers Nat.choose symmetry, via parent qBinomial_at_one.",
      "qBinomial_succ_succ_dual (dual q-Pascal) in Proofs/BinomialTheoremOQ02OQ02OQ01OQ03.lean:72",
      "qBinomial_reflection ([n,k]_q=[n,n-k]_q, k<=n) at BinomialTheoremOQ02OQ02OQ01OQ03.lean:136",
      "qBinomial_reflection_add ([a+b,a]_q=[a+b,b]_q) at line 171",
      "qBinomial_reflection_at_one_eq_choose (q=1 recovers Nat.choose_symm) at line 178"
    ],
    "insights": [
      "Both q-Pascal recurrences and reflection symmetry are governed by a single ratio invariant (q^{k+1}-1)·qBinom(n,k+1)=(q^{n-k}-1)·qBinom(n,k); proving it once unlocks dual-Pascal and reflection.",
      "The ratio invariant holds UNCONDITIONALLY (k>=n: nat-sub makes right factor q^0-1=0), removing the k<=n side condition and streamlining the induction.",
      "Reparametrising n=j+1+p eliminates ALL nat subtraction inside the induction so q-power exponents are honest sums; ring/linear_combination then close without omega gymnastics in the algebra.",
      "Reflection symmetry is subtraction-free as a statement but its proof uses q^j-1 factors, so the honest scope is CommRing not the parent CommSemiring (covers Z[q],Q(q),R,C,finite fields).",
      "Over a CommSemiring the dual q-Pascal recurrence is NOT an algebraic rearrangement of the primal one (the bridging step needs subtraction); it requires its own induction on n.",
      "Reflection symmetry needs BOTH recurrences simultaneously — dual on the left coefficient, primal on the reflected coefficient — so the surviving q-Pascal pieces become a matched pair the IH closes.",
      "Destructuring j < n as n = j+1+m clears truncated ℕ-subtraction in q-exponents (q^(n-j) -> q^(m+1)), letting ring combine powers.",
      "linear_combination is unavailable over a CommSemiring; targeted nth_rewrite of each dual relation on a single side + ring stays at CommSemiring generality."
    ],
    "mathlibGaps": [],
    "nextSteps": [
      "Full inductive q-Vandermonde identity (parent has only m=0,n=0 base cases).",
      "q-binomial theorem (Cauchy product form).",
      "Combinatorial model: [n,k]_q as partitions in a k×(n-k) box; reflection = box transpose."
    ]
  },
